UID:06mb2tat2ro61j3updpp0nmgk8@google.com
CREATED:20210311T223905Z
DESCRIPTION:\nCandidate: Dr. Joaquin Marcos Palacios\nTitle: "CPU Schedulin
 g Algorithms”\nAbstract: CPU scheduling is at the core of multiprogrammed o
 perating systems. By sharing the CPU among processes\, the computer is made
  more productive. In this talk\, we start by reviewing the basic concepts o
 f process\, process state\, and process scheduling. Then\, we describe four
  scheduling algorithms\, illustrating them with examples. For each example\
 , a scheduling metric is calculated for algorithm comparison purposes. We c
 onclude the presentation with comments on the metrics or criteria used to c
 ompare CPU scheduling algorithms.
LAST-MODIFIED:20210312T164942Z
LOCATION:https://utexas.zoom.us/j/94314012681
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:NTT Latinx Faculty Candidate Talk
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
